    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with the captured Math Academy solutions. However, q-14787 contains an error in its explanation: the region on [2,6] is not a trapezoid. Its area is a rectangle plus a triangle, 3·2+(1/2)·1·2=7. The source's incorrect geometric description nevertheless produces the correct final integral. Mathematical verification: q-114429 simplifies to −sec(x)tan(x), giving √2−2. q-114457 simplifies to −cot(x)csc(x), whose antiderivative is csc(x). q-10567 simplifies to 4x³+7csc²(3x−2π), giving x⁴−(7/3)cot(3x−2π)+C. q-13786 gives (5/4)(1−3⁻⁴)=100/81. q-113833 requires a factor of 2 from the chain rule. q-31417 requires the factor 3/ln(6). q-30973 gives (3⁶−1)/(6ln(3))=364/(3ln(3)). The signed graph areas give q-51443: −1+9/2=7/2; q-14787: 2−9/2−5−7=−29/2; q-49205: 2−2−8−2π=−2π−8. For q-40185 the graph is negative on (−∞,−3), (−2,1), and (1,∞), excluding the tangency at 1. For q-40270 the three simple roots give positivity on (−2,1) and (2,∞). For q-87672, factoring as −x²(x+3)(x−4) gives positivity on (−3,0) and (0,4). Eliminating the parameter in the selected parabola equations gives q-106447: y−2=(x+1)²/2; q-106452: y+3=−(x+2)²/10; q-106459: x+2=(y−3)²/8. These have the displayed vertices and pass through the labeled points. No submitted grades were supplied; each MA answer is established by its own captured worked solution.",
